Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: NAK bulk OUT until a receive request is armed

On EC100, boot-connected Ethernet can stop receiving when the host sends
bulk OUT traffic before the gadget netdevice opens. Delaying host traffic
until the netdevice is ready avoids the observed failure. The precise
controller failure is still unconfirmed.

Explicitly set NAK when configuring a bulk OUT endpoint, so making the
endpoint active does not rely on its previous NAK state while there is no
receive request. dwc2_hsotg_start_req() already clears NAK after
programming the receive buffer and transfer size. Leave EP0, IN and
periodic endpoints unchanged.

This is a defensive candidate for hardware validation, not a claim that
the boot-connected failure or reconnect reliability is fixed.

---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -4177,6 +4177,9 @@
 
 	case USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_BULK:
 		epctrl |= DXEPCTL_EPTYPE_BULK;
+		/* Keep OUT NAKed until start_req() installs a receive buffer. */
+		if (!dir_in)
+			epctrl |= DXEPCTL_SNAK;
 		break;
 
 	case USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_INT:
